  internal_calculus a validated command transforms a copy; the browser commits through the existing atomic revision-checked workbench store before replacing its current state
  internal_calculus canonical kilograms and explicit seconds/meters are independent of display units; paused duration and rest deadlines persist as timestamps
  internal_calculus history is the sole source of personal records and last-load prefills; a template retains its creator/program/version coordinates after member adoption
  internal_calculus the routine editor changes a copy with stable exercise and set identities; saving does not mutate active or completed snapshots and marks creator-program adaptations
  internal_calculus supersets alternate exercises within a round and delay rest until the round ends; ungrouped exercises retain their own sequence
  invariant creator selection changes presentation and available programs without changing the member coordinate or duplicating history
  invariant program exports read only selected creator routines and omit set completion; private history is exported only through the member's training-file action
  invariant connection configuration does not authorize network writes or model invocation
  invariant the local server snapshots approved assets and public program material under one content-derived version; service-worker installation admits only complete matching-version responses
  invariant an app update waits for old tabs to close; activation prunes only obsolete training app caches and never mutates member IndexedDB records
  forbidden_inference a local member identifier -> authenticated Actor identity, paid entitlement, coach consent or creator team authority
  forbidden_inference passing core tests or a Chrome offline restart -> complete openGym feature parity, verified operating-system installation, durable backup or device synchronization
  known_gap member Actor/consent, recurring terms, booking and settlement integrations remain unconnected; creator request delivery now uses native Auth and WorkGraph through a scoped creator screen
  known_gap local model requests and proposal review are implemented but disconnected in the preview; tested live Qwen1.5 output failed an equipment constraint, and live end-to-end application remains unverified
  known_gap installed application icons still use server material; member-selected studio icons apply to the browser tab
  known_gap WordPress and Frappe outputs are import files; remote acceptance and ongoing synchronization remain unverified
  known_gap exercise media and device synchronization remain to be implemented; dated multi-week plans now retain routine-version snapshots, while rescheduling and calendar reminders remain open; operating-system installation and non-Chrome offline behavior still need verification
  known_gap the OpenGym reader requires declared units, valid timestamps and supported set shapes; original schedules, additional targets and media references are retained in the export archive but not fully projected into the app
  known_gap Google Stitch generation is pending because this session exposes no browser or Stitch binding; the local surface is authored code

interaction service-site-serves-member-training
  source service-site
  destination member-training
  via components/BonfyreServiceSite/site.mjs training
  preserves member-owned storage, creator program identity, exact local asset routes and revision conflict refusal
  drops institution effects, remote writes and provider secrets
  forbids creator presentation implying access to training history or business authority

interaction member-training-reuses-browser-store
  source member-training
  destination browser-host
  via integrations/browser/extension/store.mjs
  preserves browser-local state and atomic expected-revision checks
  drops remote identity and device synchronization
  forbids a local saved record implying a native authenticated actor or paid term

architecture opengym-training-interchange
  canonical_name OpenGymTrainingInterchange
  family external
  domain External applications / Personal training data
  layer import
  semantic_question Which training facts can cross from an OpenGym state file into the member-owned training implementation without losing their original representation?
  purpose A bounded reader of the pinned public OpenGym state contract, with reviewed replacement and original training records retained for export.
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-import.mjs
  source_path packs/aurekai-fitness-studio/upstream-reference.json
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/training-import.test.mjs verifies unit, cardio, unilateral/drop, source archive and invalid-input behavior
  internal_calculus profile unit converts stored loads; cardio speed remains canonical km/h; scalar rest-pause totals are counted once and unilateral drops become explicit side-tagged rows
  invariant provider credentials and authentication state are excluded from the retained training archive
  forbidden_inference successfully importing a supported state file -> complete upstream feature parity, copied media rights, working remote synchronization or authenticated identity
  known_gap legacy records without valid start/end clocks and mixed tracking modes in one exercise are refused; media files require a separate import path

interaction opengym-state-becomes-member-training
  source opengym-training-interchange
  destination member-training
  via components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-import.mjs
  preserves stable source IDs, load units, actual completed work and original training records in a portable archive
  drops credentials and active-session execution; unprojected settings are reported in import review
  forbids replacing the member's stored history before explicit import review and a successful expected-revision write

architecture training-model-proposal
  canonical_name TrainingModelProposal
  family apps
  domain Personal applications / Training adaptation
  layer integration
  semantic_question What can a selected model propose from an explicitly reviewed exercise request, before the member chooses to apply it?
