  owns TrainingRequestBrief
  owns TrainingRequestReceipt
  owns TrainingDeliveryArtifact
  invariant native WorkGraph is the lifecycle owner; browser receipts retain access coordinates and pending briefs, not an independent completion ledger
  invariant a stable submission ID binds one immutable brief; retry cannot change its program, creator or requested work
  invariant delivered routines become visible only after native completion names their content-addressed artifact; a stale worker cannot replace the acknowledged output
  invariant newly submitted requests retain the selected public program snapshot; later catalogue changes cannot rewrite the coach's starting program
  invariant the member sends only the authored brief and selected public program reference; workout and body-weight records are not part of request intake
  forbidden_inference possession of a local request receipt or operator filesystem access -> authenticated Actor identity, coaching consent, paid entitlement or team authority
  known_gap creator request operations have native sign-in, scoped grants and reviewed public CMS publication; SLA, quoting and refusal/revision workflow remain unconnected
  known_gap claims expire after at most 24 hours and require explicit renewal; expired work is shown as needing creator attention, with recovery still performed through the native queue
  known_gap receipts and unsent briefs are local to the member browser; device synchronization and portable receipt export remain open

