  preserves live claim ownership, immutable artifact digest, expected revision and atomic stale-review refusal
  drops browser-owned revision authority and drafts from member receipt reads
  forbids a saved draft being treated as delivered or an older reviewed draft overwriting a newer saved revision

architecture training-program-publication
  experience_chain learning
  experience_chain creator-publish
  canonical_name TrainingProgramPublication
  family apps
  domain Creator operations / Program library
  layer integration
  semantic_question Which reviewed public version of a delivered routine can this studio offer without changing a member's adopted training?
  purpose Native CMS program releases with separate publishing grants, public catalogue reads, explicit adoption and version-specific withdrawal.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/training_program_release.json
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-publishing.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-publication-view.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-catalogue.mjs
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/training-publishing.test.mjs exercises native CMS persistence, namespace uniqueness, retry identity, versions, content digest checks, follow-up request snapshots and current publishing grants
  witness packs/no-simulation/fitness-studio-20261011/publishing-browser-verification.json records reviewed publication, member adoption, version preservation, offline catalogue reads, confirmed withdrawal and damaged-cache isolation
  invariant a request-scoped grant never supplies publishing permission; a delivered-request publication requires both request read access and the studio's current program write grant
  invariant CMS namespace-unique release keys admit one program version; retry identity binds the exact publication input and actor
  invariant the public projection contains the reviewed routine, title and description; private request references, member briefs, publisher credentials and actor coordinates are excluded
  invariant public routine and exercise identifiers are newly assigned; source request identifiers are not reused as public program coordinates
  invariant newly published exercise identities derive from studio, program identity and the source exercise identity; unrelated programs cannot share personal records merely by placing an exercise first
  invariant the highest program version governs catalogue visibility; withdrawing it does not resurrect an older published release
  invariant adoption copies a specific version into member-owned training; publication updates and withdrawal never mutate that copy or its workout history
  invariant public catalogue caching uses the existing browser store and never turns API responses into app assets; a damaged catalogue cannot prevent opening private training
  forbidden_inference a published public program -> paid entitlement, coaching consent, medical efficacy, remote WordPress/Frappe delivery or a right to delete member copies
  known_gap this local catalogue is bounded to 100 releases per studio and 64 KB per routine; paging, media, paid-tier publication and dedicated MCP operations remain open
  known_gap withdrawal reaches a disconnected catalogue on its next successful refresh; downloaded and adopted public material remains on the member device

interaction training-creator-publishes-cms-program
  source training-creator-access
  destination training-program-publication
  via components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-creator.mjs /studios/STUDIO/programs
  preserves native actor binding, separate current publishing grant, reviewed public fields, stable retry identity and expected program version
  drops permission inferred from coaching assignment and automatic publication after delivery
  forbids a publication review screen or completed coaching request counting as a published release

interaction training-program-release-uses-native-cms
  source training-program-publication
  destination cmd-c-m-s
  via components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-publishing.mjs schema apply and namespace-scoped entry create/list/update
  preserves native content records, unique release and publication keys, publication state and private provenance
  drops a second application-owned publication database or direct SQL mutations from the training server
  forbids a request receipt or local JSON file acting as public catalogue truth

interaction member-training-adopts-published-program
  source member-training
  destination training-program-publication
  via components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-catalogue.mjs and /api/training/programs/STUDIO
  preserves exact public program version, studio scope, offline public cache and explicit local adoption
  drops private request metadata and authority to rewrite already adopted routines
  forbids catalogue refresh or withdrawal deleting or changing the member's routines and workouts

architecture training-program-authoring
  experience_chain learning
  experience_chain creator-publish
  canonical_name TrainingProgramAuthoring
  domain MemberTraining
  family apps
  semantic_question How can a studio editor build and retain its own routine without a member request or permission to read client work?
  purpose Studio program library authoring with native CMS edit history and reviewed public releases
  maturity implemented
  internal_calculus normalized routine drafts, revision digest comparison in native SQL, scoped program grants and publication revision checks
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/training_program_draft.json
