  witness packs/no-simulation/fitness-studio-20261011/library-browser-verification.json records library-only sign-in, authoring, reopening, two-tab conflict recovery, stale review refusal, publication and member adoption
  invariant library writes require the studio's current program write grant and never infer access to member requests
  invariant a content digest includes the draft revision; native compare-and-update admits one writer against that saved revision
  invariant retries of the same saved revision, routine and actor are idempotent; conflicting edits remain available in the browser
  invariant publication checks the reviewed saved revision and copies its routine into a separate release; later source edits cannot change the release
  invariant native CMS edit history retains successful draft updates without an application-owned history table
  forbidden_inference a saved program draft -> published content, paid entitlement, consent to personal training records or offline creator editing
  known_gap the local library is bounded to 100 draft entries and 64 KB per routine; paging, draft archival, revision browsing and offline creator editing remain open

interaction training-program-authoring-uses-native-cms
  source training-program-authoring
  destination cmd-c-m-s
  via native entry create and entry update --if-field content_sha --if-value EXPECTED
  preserves studio namespace, normalized routine, revision digest, edit identity and native operation history
  drops direct SQL writes and browser-owned publication authority
  forbids stale client state replacing the latest draft or successful saving implying publication

interaction training-program-authoring-publishes-review
  source training-program-authoring
  destination training-program-publication
  via /studios/STUDIO/programs with draftId and draftRevision
  preserves reviewed source revision, explicit publication action and independently versioned release
  drops a requirement to create a member request before library authoring
  forbids editing a draft from changing a previously published or adopted version

